<title>AUSTRALIA: RTRS-Adelaide Brighton sells Humes NZ.</title>
<headline>RTRS-Adelaide Brighton sells Humes NZ.</headline>
<text>
<p>ADELAIDE, Dec 23 (Retuer) - Adelaide Brighton Ltd said on Monday it had sold its Humes Pipe businesses in New Zealand for a little more than NZ$58 million.</p>
<p>The company said Humes Steelpipe Ltd was acquired by HSP Investments Ltd with the remainder of the businesses, excluding Hurricane Wire Products, bought by Firth Industries Ltd, a subsidiary of Fletcher Challenge Building.</p>
<p>It said the sale price would result in a surplus over book value, with the sales to be completed on December 31.</p>
<p>Funds would be used to reduced existing debt.</p>
<p>-- Sydney Newsroom 61-2 9373-1800</p>
